<h2>A demanding but substantial market</h2>
<p>Germany is Europe's largest economy and a leading destination for Indian psyllium husk, guar gum, dehydrated onion and turmeric — products that feed its large pharmaceutical, dietary-supplement and food-manufacturing sectors.</p>

<h2>Expect rigorous compliance expectations</h2>
<p>German importers, operating within the shared EU regulatory framework, are widely known for particularly thorough documentation and quality-assurance expectations. This isn't a different rulebook from the rest of the EU, but it often means a more detailed conversation about testing, traceability and certificates of analysis than some other European markets.</p>
<p>We'd recommend preparing your quality documentation proactively for a German enquiry rather than reactively. {{ site.complianceChecklistCta }}</p>

<h2>Psyllium husk and guar gum: pharmaceutical-grade considerations</h2>
<p>A meaningful share of German demand for psyllium husk and guar gum feeds pharmaceutical and dietary-supplement manufacturing, which can carry tighter purity and contamination specifications than food-grade use. Tell us the end-use application and we'll confirm what grade and testing is appropriate.</p>

